le-body article-body--flush custom-cs-body min-w-0 text-[1.125rem] leading-[1.75]"}><p className={"text-[clamp(1.25rem,1.1rem_+_0.5vw,1.5rem)] leading-[1.55] text-text"}>{"Corvane sells homeware to about 60,000 customers a month. Behind every order sat a chain of people copying numbers from one tab to another."}</p><p>{"Daniel Hart joined as Head of Operations in 2023 and counted forty hand-offs between the shop, the warehouse, support and finance. Most of them were a person reading one screen and typing into another. Month-end took four working days, and support answered the same “where is my order?” question two hundred times a week."}</p><h2>{"One wall, then one canvas"}</h2><p>{"Daniel and Priya, who runs finance operations, spent a morning putting every hand-off on a wall in sticky notes. Anything that followed a rule became a candidate for a workflow. Anything that needed judgement got a person — and an approval step."}</p><figure className={"custom-photo custom-cs-photo"} style={{"--custom-photo-ratio": "16 / 10"}}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/framo/assets/media/placeholder/1600x900.svg"} alt={"A finance lead frowns at a spreadsheet of unmatched invoices on her tablet"} width={"1600"} height={"900"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption className={"absolute left-4 bottom-4 m-0 py-1.5 px-3.5 text-[0.9375rem] bg-surface rounded-pill text-text"}>{"Before: invoices matched by hand, one line at a time."}</figcaption></figure><h2>{"What they built first"}</h2><p>{"The first workflow took a week. Every supplier invoice is read on arrival, matched to its purchase order and posted to the ledger. Anything that doesn't match, or comes in over $5,000, waits for Priya in team chat."}</p><figure className={"custom-cs-flow"}><ol className={"custom-panel custom-teams-flow custom-so-flow m-0"} aria-label={"Corvane's invoice workflow"}><li className={"custom-node"}><span className={"custom-glyph"} style={{"--custom-glyph": "#475569"}}><i className={"ph-bold ph-envelope-simple"}></i></span><span className={"grid gap-[0.1875rem] min-w-0"}><b className={"custom-node-title"}>{"Invoice received"}</b><span className={"custom-node-meta"}>{"Inbox"}</span></span></li><li className={"custom-node"}><span className={"custom-glyph custom-glyph--brand"}><i className={"ph-bold ph-sparkle"}></i></span><span className={"grid gap-[0.1875rem] min-w-0"}><b className={"custom-node-title"}>{"Match PO "}<span className={"custom-node-ai"}>{"AI"}</span></b><span className={"custom-node-meta"}>{"Framo Agent"}</span></span></li><li className={"custom-node"}><span className={"custom-glyph"} style={{"--custom-glyph": "#1f8a5b"}}><i className={"ph-bold ph-book-open-text"}></i></span><span className={"grid gap-[0.1875rem] min-w-0"}><b className={"custom-node-title"}>{"Post to ledger"}</b><span className={"custom-node-meta"}>{"Accounting"}</span></span></li></ol><figcaption className={"text-start"}>{"The invoice workflow: 96% of invoices go straight through."}</figcaption></figure><p>{"Support came next. An agent now reads every new ticket, finds the order and drafts a reply with the tracking link. The team checks and sends — or lets it send on its own for the simplest questions."}</p><blockquote className={"custom-cs-quote relative pt-12 pb-0 px-0"}><p className={"font-heading text-[clamp(1.5rem,1.2rem_+_1vw,2rem)] font-semibold leading-[1.3] tracking-[-0.025em]"}>{"Nobody here writes code for a living. We built sixty workflows anyway, because everyone could read what the last person made."}</p><cite>{"Daniel Hart, Head of Operations"}</cite></blockquote><h2>{"The results"}</h2><p>{"A year in, Corvane runs sixty workflows and three agents. Month-end closes in an afternoon, support triages 92% of tickets automatically, and the team gets 38 hours back every week — time Daniel says now goes on suppliers and customers, not tabs."}</p><p>{"Next on the wall: returns, and a weekly stock report the warehouse has asked for since 2022."}</p></article></div></di